From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:54:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: offer HDMI 3D modes only on TMDS outputs to HDMI
 sinks

The HDMI 1.4a 3D structures are signalled by the HDMI vendor InfoFrame
(HDMI 1.4a, section 8.2.3), which nv50_hdmi_enable() sends only from a SOR
driving TMDS to a sink whose EDID makes it HDMI. Stereo has been allowed
on DisplayPort connectors since commit 0f18d2765ab1 ("drm/nouveau: Enable
stereoscopic 3D output over HDMI"), so that a DP++ adaptor, which nouveau
drives through the connector's TMDS encoder, gets HDMI 3D. But the 3D
modes of a sink's HDMI VSDB were then listed whatever the connector
drove: a native DisplayPort sink with an HDMI VSDB, and the HDMI sink
behind a DP-to-HDMI protocol converter, got HDMI 3D modes checked against
the DisplayPort link (nv50_dp_mode_valid()) and sent with nothing to tell
the sink, as nouveau sends no DisplayPort SDP at all. A DVI sink, which
takes no InfoFrame, was in the same place on any connector.

Refuse the HDMI 3D layouts, every stereo layout but frame sequential,
unless the detected encoder is a SOR driving TMDS and the sink is HDMI:
nouveau_connector_mode_valid() returns MODE_NO_STEREO, so the modes are
no longer listed, and nv50_outp_atomic_check() returns -EINVAL, so an
atomic commit of such a mode fails too. External TMDS transmitters
(PIORs) get no InfoFrame either and are refused the same way. Frame
sequential is DisplayPort's own stereo and is refused by the DRM core
until nouveau opts in.

The DP++ case that commit 0f18d2765ab1 enabled keeps its 3D modes; the
others never switched a sink into 3D.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c     |  5 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c |  4 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.h | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
index 1771a08aa..1358b8d41 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
@@ -530,6 +530,11 @@ nv50_outp_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	struct nv50_head_atom *asyh = nv50_head_atom(crtc_state);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (nouveau_mode_is_hdmi_3d(&crtc_state->mode) &&
+	    !nouveau_connector_hdmi_3d_signalled(nouveau_encoder(encoder),
+						 &connector->display_info))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	ret = nv50_outp_atomic_check_view(encoder, crtc_state, conn_state,
 					  nv_connector->native_mode);
 	if (ret)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
index 5128a6a69..32e8df40f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
@@ -1114,6 +1114,10 @@ nouveau_connector_mode_valid(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	struct drm_encoder *encoder = to_drm_encoder(nv_encoder);
 	unsigned int min_clock = 25000, max_clock = min_clock, clock = mode->clock;
 
+	if (nouveau_mode_is_hdmi_3d(mode) &&
+	    !nouveau_connector_hdmi_3d_signalled(nv_encoder, &connector->display_info))
+		return MODE_NO_STEREO;
+
 	/* Reject modes exceeding the postcomp viewport limit where scaler
 	 * limits are enforced. Atomic check applies the same limit.
 	 */
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.h
index 742d00f49..8ca5eb106 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.h
@@ -173,6 +173,30 @@ nouveau_connector_is_mst(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	return encoder->encoder_type == DRM_MODE_ENCODER_DPMST;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The HDMI 1.4a 3D structures are signalled by the HDMI vendor InfoFrame
+ * (section 8.2.3), which nv50_hdmi_enable() sends from an on-chip TMDS output
+ * (a SOR) to an HDMI sink only: on an HDMI connector, or on a DisplayPort
+ * connector through a DP++ adaptor. A DisplayPort sink, a DVI sink, or an
+ * external TMDS transmitter (a PIOR) would get the 3D timing with nothing to
+ * tell the sink.
+ */
+static inline bool
+nouveau_connector_hdmi_3d_signalled(const struct nouveau_encoder *nv_encoder,
+				    const struct drm_display_info *info)
+{
+	return nv_encoder && nv_encoder->dcb &&
+	       nv_encoder->dcb->type == DCB_OUTPUT_TMDS &&
+	       nv_encoder->outp.info.type == NVIF_OUTP_SOR && info->is_hdmi;
+}
+
+/* the HDMI 3D layouts: every stereo layout but frame sequential */
+static inline bool
+nouveau_mode_is_hdmi_3d(const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	return drm_mode_is_stereo(mode) && !drm_mode_is_frame_sequential(mode);
+}
+
 #define nouveau_for_each_non_mst_connector_iter(connector, iter) \
 	drm_for_each_connector_iter(connector, iter) \
 		for_each_if(!nouveau_connector_is_mst(connector))
-- 
